# This repository is a documentation tree: guides, configs and the images and
# firmware they reference. It had no .gitignore at all, which is how deleted
# klippy logs, resonance CSVs, a video and an 80 MB CAD assembly ended up in
# its history, where git keeps them forever.
#
# None of the patterns below match anything currently tracked. Genuinely
# needed binaries go through Git LFS instead, as the eMMC backup under
# printers/qidiq1pro/ already does; add a .gitattributes beside the file
# rather than committing it raw.

# Klipper and printer run-time output. Regenerated constantly, large, and of
# no use to a reader of the guides.
*.log
klippy.log*
klippy.log.*
*.gcode
*.gco

# Input shaper and resonance testing output.
resonances_*.csv
calibration_data_*.csv
adxl345-*.csv
*.csv

# Video. Use a link rather than committing it.
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi
*.webm

# CAD working files. Large, opaque to diff, and not readable as documentation.
# The tracked Trident assembly predates this rule.
*.f3z
*.step
*.stp
*.3mf

# Archives, other than the LFS-tracked backups that carry their own
# .gitattributes.
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.xz

# Editor and OS clutter.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
